    "bio": "a Representative from Virginia; born near Warrenton, Fauquier County, Va., birth date unknown; member of the Virginia state house of delegates, 1798-1804; delegate to the Virginia state constitutional convention in 1829 and 1830; elected as a Democratic Republican to the Twelfth and to the five succeeding Congresses; reelected as a Crawford Republican to the Eighteenth Congress; and reelected as a Jacksonian candidate to the Nineteenth and to the three succeeding Congresses (March 4, 1811-March 3, 1833); chairman, Committee on Claims (Twentieth Congress); died in Charlottesville, Va., in 1864; interment in the University of Virginia Cemetery.",
